            <ArticleTitle>Huge left atrial thrombus with mitral stenosis in congenital factor XII deficiency.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>286-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Factor XII deficiency has been reported to be a risk factor for thromboembolism as a result of inactivation of fibrinolysis. We describe a case of a huge left atrial thrombus with mitral stenosis, which was successfully removed surgically in a Factor XII deficient patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
